# Day 34 Reflection

Today I learned that web applications are one of the most common targets for attackers.

The biggest lesson was understanding the differences between SQL Injection, Cross-Site Scripting, and Cross-Site Request Forgery. I also learned that many of these attacks can be prevented through proper input validation, secure coding, and regular application testing.

As a future cybersecurity analyst, understanding application attacks will help me identify vulnerabilities before attackers can exploit them.
